ONE modification has been made to the vendored formula, and exactly one. On
2026-08-24 the Grade-A aggregate rule's second clause was changed from
`mean - stdev >= POOLED_LOWER_BOUND (105)` to
`mean - CONFIDENCE_K (1.0) * stdev/sqrt(n) >= POOLED_TARGET (108)` by a recorded
decision, docs/adr/0006-confidence-bound-on-the-pooled-mean.md, after the
retired clause was demonstrated to change a verdict on a byte-identical file.
FLOORS, POOLED_TARGET, MIN_ROUNDS, AGG_METHOD, RUBRIC_SHA, INDEPENDENT_METHODS
and every other function in the file are as vendored. This repository and its
upstream therefore DIVERGE in that one clause, deliberately and on the record;
a score quoted across the two must name which rule produced it. Apart from that
clause, only repo-specific glue (skill-name sets, file paths, environment
variable name) was adapted for this repository, as itemized per file in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. The upstream eval-harness repository does not endorse
and is not affiliated with this repository.

